WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.180
- [Presenter] This 128
foot long super yacht

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:06.060
runs almost $14 million to purchase,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.673
but that's just the
beginning of its expenses.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.290
- [James] It's a city, it's
a resort, and it moves.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.360
- [Presenter] But imagine
if that resort sat on top

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.450
of one of the planet's
saltiest, wettest environments.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.520
Yacht owners can also expect to pay

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.280
10 to 20% of the yachts value each year

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.050
simply to maintain it.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.990
Superyachts or yachts longer than 82 feet

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.660
can sell for hundreds
of millions of dollars.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.560
This means maintenance could
be tens of millions per year.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.360
Here's what goes into this superyacht's

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.423
estimated annual budget
of nearly 1.9 million.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:43.500
- [James] Welcome aboard Snowbird.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.219
- [Presenter] Cost that up
even before owner set sail.

00:00:46.219 --> 00:00:48.120
- [James] Dockage fees are very expensive.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.440
They range from $3.50 a
foot to 7.50 a foot per day.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.690
- [Presenter] Dockage fees
can be so high for superyachts

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:56.520
in part because there's a large demand

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.380
for a limited number of spaces,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.270
but if owners keep their yachts docked,

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.670
they could face other
large maintenance expenses.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:05.550
- All the works of the
bottom of the vessel

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.790
gets scummed up with oysters
and clams and barnacles.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.200
A lot of these electronics,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.170
they get fouled up if they
sit dormant for a long time.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.960
It's definitely better to
use it than let it sit.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.793
- [Presenter] While docked,

00:01:16.793 --> 00:01:18.720
the yacht can connect to
the Marina's power grid

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.280
for basic operations,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.870
but when it's out at sea, this
368 ton vessel requires fuel,

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:25.703
a lot of it.

00:01:25.703 --> 00:01:28.070
- For someone like myself,
I call this boat yoga.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.810
What we have here is the day tank.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:34.230
This holds approximately
800 gallons of fuel.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.160
See the red?

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.140
That's the amount that's in the tank.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:37.973
- [Presenter] In total,

00:01:37.973 --> 00:01:41.190
this yacht can hold almost
12,000 gallons of fuel.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.950
Plus, other water
vehicles like its jet skis

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:46.650
and support boat will need even more gas.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.360
- Generally, we burn anywhere

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.960
from 60 gallons an hour
to 120 gallons an hour.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.820
- [Presenter] At around four
and a half dollars a gallon.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.570
- [James] It costs
approximately $360,000 per year

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.740
to fuel Snowbird.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:01:59.880
- [Presenter] But day-to-day maintenance

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.940
is actually the fourth
largest operating cost

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.500
and it can get messy.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.910
- Today we're gonna be changing out

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.710
the crankcase ventilation filter.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.560
That keeps your turbos
and your after cooler

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.790
from getting gummed up,

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.340
and it also helps reduce oil consumption

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.290
and reduce air pollution

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.930
by further combustion inside the engine.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:21.930
This part probably costs
$60, $70 to replace,

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.270
but it has immeasurable value

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:27.240
in prolonging the
longevity of your motors.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.820
Maintaining the engines
on a yacht like Snowbird

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.000
typically costs around $60,000 a year,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.880
and you're looking at parts, time,

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.210
and the materials involved
to change the oils

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.220
and keep everything up and going.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:42.690
- [Presenter] That's just below deck.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.730
Superyacht owners also need to invest

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.580
in keeping the rest of the
yacht in pristine condition,

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:49.110
like the teak flooring.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.760
Teak is typically used on yachts

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.310
because it's a weather
resistant luxury material,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.830
but it's also challenging to maintain.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.910
- [Josh] When we scrub the teak,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.000
oftentimes it only lasts
roughly a week or two

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.590
depending on the traffic on board.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.360
It wants to go back to its natural color,

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.270
and, you know, between
rain and rinsing it down,

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.890
you kinda wash away all of that,

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.260
you know, hard work that you've done.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.220
Annually the teak flooring
costs about $18,000 to maintain.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.780
- [Presenter] Adding on smaller expenses,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.960
you're already looking
at just over $1 million.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.230
But by far, there's one cost
for maintaining superyachts

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.203
that completely surpasses
the others, the crew.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.740
The estimated budget for Snowbird's crew

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:32.970
is over $800,000 per year and
that's because super yachts

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.880
must always have a crew even when docked.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.140
- You have to take care of the teak

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:40.110
the paint, wash windows, machinery.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.110
Rust never sleeps,
maintenance never stops.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.060
- [Presenter] Cost towards
their health insurance,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.990
travel expenses, uniforms,
and cell phone bills

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:51.150
can add thousands to the budget.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.560
Adding in crew expenses

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.690
brings the annual operating cost estimate

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.570
to nearly 1.9 million a year,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.940
but that's only when
there are no major repairs

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:01.350
or maintenance

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.960
while owners generally
spend around 10% a year

00:04:03.960 --> 00:04:06.600
in maintenance costs for new superyachts.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.920
- [James] It's kind of a guideline,

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.200
but as she gets three years or five years,

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.050
or hits her 10 year, it's
gonna be more than 10%.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:14.550
- [Presenter] Every five years or so,

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.350
superyacht owners have to shell out

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.510
for one of their largest expenses.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.090
- Paint jobs are sometimes
from a hundred thousand

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.880
to a million bucks, depending
on your size of your boat.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:26.760
Paint is about $1,800 an inch,

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.290
- [Presenter] Salt in the water and air

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:29.970
corrodes the yachts paint.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.740
To repaint the entire yacht,

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.750
it needs to be hauled out of the water,

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:36.990
then it can take months to
complete a fresh paint job.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:39.750
There are also other
major potential expenses.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.220
Some yacht owners need to spend

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.710
hundreds of thousands of
dollars every few years

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.390
on detailed inspections.

00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:47.280
And if a yacht fails in inspection,

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:51.540
repairing or replacing it
could run $200,000 or more.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.880
- Certain boats, you
can't get the engines out.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.650
You have to cut a hole in the side

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.720
and then reweld it, recertify the hole.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:01.740
Now you're into the multi-millions
to change out an engine.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.420
- [Presenter] To recoup
some of these costs,

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.120
superyacht owners will
rent out their vessels.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.770
The charter fee for this super yacht

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:12.120
ranges from $125 to $145,000 per week,

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.920
that covers the boat and the crew,

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.650
but renters also need to
pay for additional expenses

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.410
like fuel, food, and customs fees.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:21.090
Plus, there's a customary tip

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.180
of 18 to 25% for the crew members.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.800
At best, superyacht owners

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:27.630
might break-even on maintenance costs

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.490
with income earned from chartering.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.560
- I don't think it's a
profitable situation.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:34.170
At best, they're covering their salaries

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:36.090
and the boat's way as it travels.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:37.350
Wear and tear is always there

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.540
and the money would have
to go back into the vessel.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:42.210
If you didn't properly
maintain your vessel,

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.800
your value would decrease.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:47.340
Most people that buy yachts
of this size and this stature

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:48.767
really wanna take care of them.

00:05:48.767 --> 00:05:51.350
(upbeat music)

